-- title:
--   Extracting Fourier coefficients through tagged frames
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that a real Banach space $X$ with the approximation property is K-convex (the Rademacher projection is bounded on $L_2(\{\pm1\}^n;X)$ uniformly in $n$) if and only if $X$ and its dual $X^*$ both have finite cotype. The converse direction shows that such $X$ has nontrivial type, i.e. does not contain $\ell_1^n$ uniformly, and then derives K-convexity from a power-gap estimate for commuting coordinate projections. Fix growth pairing data with lifts $P$ and $Z$.
--
--   1. **Free pairing pattern.** For tuples $u,v$ in $\{0,1\}^k$, the sign matrix of their $\mathbb F_2$ pairings, $S_{ij}=\langle v_j,u_i\rangle$.
--   2. **Coefficient primal.** $P$ applied to the tagged primal tuple $(u_i,e_i,0)$.
--   3. **Coefficient dual.** For a frequency $P$,
--   $$
--   \mathbb E_D\,w_P(D)\;Z_{\tilde V(D)}(\delta),
--   $$
--   averaging dual lifts over the sign matrices $D$ encoded in the tags. Pairing these extracts the Fourier coefficient $\hat\Psi(P)$ of the pattern function as an actual operator pairing.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Cotype/TaggedCoefficient.lean

